# Vulnerabilities in Node.js base image bundled npm packages.
# These are transitive dependencies inside /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/
# and are not used by our application code. They are fixed when the Node.js
# base image is updated.

# minimatch ReDoS — in npm's bundled glob, not our dependency
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# picomatch — in npm's bundled dependency, not ours
CVE-2026-33671
CVE-2026-33672

# brace-expansion DoS — in npm's bundled minimatch, not ours
CVE-2026-33750

# sigstore accepts unauthorized certificates (ignored `certificateOIDs`) — in
# npm's bundled sigstore at /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/sigstore,
# used by `npm audit signatures` / provenance verification. It is absent from our
# package-lock.json and never invoked by application code at runtime.
# Unlike the entries above, this one is NOT yet fixed by updating the base image:
# node:22-alpine (latest, verified 2026-07-18) still bundles sigstore 3.1.0, and
# the fix landed in 4.1.1. Re-check and remove this entry once a Node base image
# ships npm with sigstore >= 4.1.1.
CVE-2026-48815
